From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:26:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg/FmpDeviceSmmLib: Only the regions the platform
 allows

[ouroBIOS: patches/edk2/0045, without the files that TianoCore's tree
does not have (tools/edk2-import.py): 1 in edk2/OuroBiosPkg]

The library writes every region that the manifest of a signed capsule
names, through the SMMSTORE handler, which serves the whole flash on a
boot with update capsules: a capsule built wrong, naming the variable
store, the vital product data or the GbE region of the descriptor, is
written as it says. And on a flash with the two RW slots of vboot only
a manifest with both is written one slot at a time: one with a slot
alone writes that slot whether it runs or not, and leaves vboot nothing
to fall back to.

Add PcdFmpDeviceSmmAllowedRegions, the names of the regions that an
update may write: the image check, and the write before it writes
anything, refuse a manifest with another region, with
LAST_ATTEMPT_STATUS_SMMSTORE_INVALID_IMAGE. A list without names, the
default, allows every region, as before. The platform allows the two
slots and RW_MRC_CACHE, the regions of the capsules of ouroBIOS. A
flash with both slots takes only a manifest with both, or refuses the
image the same way.

FmpDeviceSmmManifest.h includes UefiBaseType.h for EFI_STATUS, so that
FmpDeviceSmmVboot.c builds in the host unit test too.

TEST=The host unit tests (UefiPayloadPkg/Test/UefiPayloadPkgHostTest.dsc),
19 of 19: the regions of the release capsules allowed in any order;
SMMSTORE, SI_GBE, a prefix or a longer name refused; a list without
names allowing every region; a flash with both slots taking only a
manifest with both. FmpDxe built with the library (DEBUG, X64).
---
diff --git a/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/FmpDeviceSmmLib/FmpDeviceSmmLib.c b/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/FmpDeviceSmmLib/FmpDeviceSmmLib.c
index 2e7c347..a707531 100644
--- a/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/FmpDeviceSmmLib/FmpDeviceSmmLib.c
+++ b/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/FmpDeviceSmmLib/FmpDeviceSmmLib.c
@@ -6,17 +6,20 @@
   SMMSTORE handler, which serves the whole flash on a boot that starts with
   update capsules.  The image must carry an RMAP manifest (appended by
   AppendRmapManifest.py) naming the FMAP regions to write; each of them must
-  be where the running firmware's FMAP has it.  Everything else, in particular
-  the regions written once per machine (the variable store, vital product
-  data, event log) and the regions the flash descriptor protects, stays as it
-  is.  An image without a manifest, or for another flash layout, is refused:
-  such a firmware is installed with an external tool.
+  be where the running firmware's FMAP has it, and one of the regions that
+  PcdFmpDeviceSmmAllowedRegions lets an update write, if it names any.
+  Everything else, in particular the regions written once per machine (the
+  variable store, vital product data, event log) and the regions the flash
+  descriptor protects, stays as it is.  An image without a manifest, or for
+  another flash layout, is refused: such a firmware is installed with an
+  external tool.
 
   A manifest with the two RW slots of vboot (RW_SECTION_A and RW_SECTION_B)
   updates only the slot that is not running, with the other regions it
   names, then asks vboot, in its nvdata in RW_NVRAM, to try that slot on the
   next boots: an update cut short, or a slot that does not verify or boot,
-  leaves the old slot to boot from.
+  leaves the old slot to boot from.  A flash with both slots is only
+  updated that way: a manifest without them, or with one alone, is refused.
 
